zig-out/
zig-cache/
.zig-cache/
.zig-cache-global/
.zig-cache-local/
zig-pkg/
*.o
# Toolchain version is pinned by build.zig.zon (minimum_zig_version) + the global
# mise default; a per-checkout .mise.toml is a personal override, never committed.
.mise.toml
/dist/
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
*.log
.tmp/
node_modules/
# Build outputs only — ui/agentsfleet.dev/dist is a committed static site, not a build artifact
cli/dist/
ui/packages/*/dist/
coverage/
.next/
**/.next/
playwright-report/
playwright-results/
playwright-tests/
playwright-acceptance-report/
playwright-acceptance-results/
playwright-auth-results/
.fixture-jwts.json
.vercel-bypass-state.json
test-results/
blob-report/
.playwright-mcp/
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
scratch_pad.md
**/scratch_pad.md
.claude/worktrees/
.context/
# orly materialises four skills per host. .agents/ and .opencode/ commit
# theirs; .claude/ ignored its own, so `orly doctor` failed in CI against a
# checkout missing files .oracle/orly.json declares managed. Everything orly
# writes is meant to be committed. Locally-added Claude skills stay ignored.
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/orly-babysit-prs/
!.claude/skills/orly-spec-new/
!.claude/skills/orly-write-integration-test/
!.claude/skills/orly-write-unit-test/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
agentsfleet/docs/spec/new-feature.md
__pycache__/
.gstack/

# Rust build output. `rustd/Cargo.lock` IS committed: the workspace builds a
# daemon binary, and an application pins its dependency graph so a rebuild months
# from now resolves what was tested, not whatever has since been published.
rustd/target/

# Coverage report written by `make test-coverage-rustd`.
rustd/lcov.info
